Author: David Gauchard <gauchard@laas.fr>
Date: 2019-03-22 13:56:13 +0100
Subject: fix d-a-v/esp82xx-nonos-linklayer#31

using external hook w/o extra lwipopts flag
remove the hook in case this needs disabling

modified 2.0.x patch, randomize tcp_port just once and preserve the increment logic
note that esp-lwip, which was used as reference, no longer uses randomization

also note that upstream lwip apparently never checks the range outside of this block
moved tcp_port++ back into if-expression, so the randomized value doesnt overflow

Signed-off-by: Maxim Prokhorov <prokhorov.max@outlook.com>

---
 src/core/tcp.c |    7 +++++--
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/core/tcp.c b/src/core/tcp.c
index 371db2b62..8c2521895 100644
--- a/src/core/tcp.c
+++ b/src/core/tcp.c
@@ -1015,9 +1015,12 @@ tcp_new_port(void)
   u16_t n = 0;
   struct tcp_pcb *pcb;
 
+#ifndef LWIP_HOOK_TCP_NEW_PORT
+#define LWIP_HOOK_TCP_NEW_PORT(PORT) (void)(PORT)
+#endif
+  LWIP_HOOK_TCP_NEW_PORT(tcp_port);
 again:
-  tcp_port++;
-  if (tcp_port == TCP_LOCAL_PORT_RANGE_END) {
+  if (tcp_port++ == TCP_LOCAL_PORT_RANGE_END) {
     tcp_port = TCP_LOCAL_PORT_RANGE_START;
   }
   /* Check all PCB lists. */
